<title>EGYPT: Egypt bank raises 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>Egypt bank raises 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit International d'Egypte/CIE said on Monday it was paying a dividend of 24.50 pounds ($7.22) for calendar 1996, against 14.00 for 1995.</p>
<p>Credit Commercial de France (CCF) became majority sharehholder in CIE last year by buying a large stake from state-owned National Bank of Egypt.</p>
<p>Shares in CIE closed on the Egyptian stock exchange last week at 710.00 pounds.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
